Live-draw: CPU-visible ZPASS report values from the occlusion queries (asynchronous readback).

Symptom: a title that reads its occlusion reports back (Killzone 3's coronas: CoronaResource QueryOffset /
FadeInTime / FadeOutTime) always saw "visible": the walker writes 0xFFFF into every type-1 GET_REPORT, so a
light behind a wall kept its glow at full intensity. Patch 2025 used the queries only for GPU predication.

Fix: at GET_REPORT, a report with exactly one query segment since its clear is also resolved into a READBACK
buffer ring (4096 x u64, mapped for good). Entries get the queue fence value at the next submit; the end of
every flush copies the counts whose fence has passed into the guest report (value at IO offset + 8,
big-endian). No wait anywhere (the present flush already waits for frame N-1, so counts land a frame later).
Walk-time value: 0 when no draw ran since the clear, else the report's last read-back count, else 0xFFFF.
Off: LD_COND_RENDER=0 (all of 2025 + 2027) or LD_OQ_READBACK=0 (this part). Log every 256 flips:
"[report-readback] flips= queued= written= zero= dropped= never= walk-last=".

Verified with tools/smoke/test_cond_render.c (host test under Proton, main-memory report context).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, the 2013 helper is gone (PR256), upstream main-memory test inlined.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): report readback moved into upstream's gcm_3d_method.

